    "prompt_additions": "Tonga Acts use PART > SECTION as the standard hierarchy. Complex Acts (e.g., tax, financial) also use DIVISION between PART and SECTION (PART > DIVISION > SECTION). Use DIVISION only when explicitly present in the source document. Constitution uses PART > SECTION (Clauses map to SECTION). Subsidiary legislation uses SECTION for individual regulations (REGULATION is not a Bluebell keyword). The enacting formula is: 'Be it enacted by the King and Legislative Assembly of Tonga in the Legislature of the Kingdom as follows:'"
